  "details": "Title says it all.\n\nnavigating the camera UI to change pins on desktop is rather tedious and time-consuming, especially when we talk about audiovisual events. it takes about 5-10 seconds of my hand-time to navigate the UI, open the stream camera, chose pin, click said pin, then close the camera ui again. \n\nthis is not desirable in the context of live-events, too much time wasted. a simple keybind to an F-key or a numpad number would make it so much more efficient (a fraction of a second) \n\nideally give us the option to choose which buttons triggers the change, so we can use macro or hardware-midi controller to do this.\n\nthis aligns well with the current effort of the dolly system too, you could make 3 different dollies and toggle between them (ideally at the beginning of the animation)\n\nthis also means everyone benefits from it, desktop users don't need to mess around opening the UI just to change a pin, vr user can use macros on third-party hardware to change their cam without aligning the laser in the ui.",
